  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\nNo Known Allergies / Adverse Drug Reactions\n\nChief Complaint:\nScheduled Chemotherapy\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nAs per admitting MD\nMr. ___ is a pleasant ___ w/ T1DM, CAD, ICM LVEF 40%, HTN, \nDL,\nAdrenal insufficiency, and AML t(8;31) s/p 7+3 induction \nfollowed\nby C2 MiDAC consolidation, who presents for C3. Pt has no acute\ncomplaints. He was seen by Dr ___ cleared him for\nchemo. He denied any dyspnea, no ___, no CP/SOB, no N/V. He does\nhave a right heel pressure ulceration that is tender on\nambulation.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\n___ w/ T1DM, CAD, ICM (LVEF 40%), HTN, Adrenal insufficiency, \nand AML t(8;31) s/p 7+3 induction followed by C2 MiDAC \nconsolidation, who presented for C3 which he tolerated well with \nthe exception of hyper/hypoglycemia\n\n#Nighttime hypoxia\nPatient noted to be hypoxic at night requiring O2 during stay. \nHe noted that this is a chronic issue for him and has nighttime \nnasal cannula use at home (2L). Given such findings, I would \nrec'd outpatient sleep study to assess whether he has OSA and \nneeds CPAP/BIPAP in addition to nasal cannula\n\n# AML\nEnrolled into ___ \"A Randomized Phase ___ Clinical Trial of \nDendritic Cell/AML Fusion cell vaccine versus DC/AML fusion cell \nvaccine in conjunction with Durvalumab, versus observation in \npatients who achieve a chemotherapy-induced remission\". \nAdmitting attending reviewed the elevated LDH with BMT attending \nwho cleared him to proceed with MiDAC C3 which he tolerated well \nwith the exception of hyper/hypoglycemia due to dexamethasone \ngiven as part of regimen. ___ team followed along and made \ndaily adjustments to insulin regimen as a result.\n\nOf note, patient had persistent end gaze nystagmus which \nextinguished after several beats, had slight dysmetria noted on \nboth hands, and extremely poor handwriting (baseline), which he \nfelt was chronic/unchanged, remained unchanged during course, so \nDr ___ elected to continue/complete regimen as planned\n\nAs per Dr ___ was discharged with plan to have \nclinic apt and receive Neulasta on ___. Patient knows to \ncontinue prednisolone eye drops for 48 hrs post chemo. He was \ndischarged on daily levofloxacin prophylaxis in light of heel \nulcer and recent neutropenic fever, with final duration to be \ndetermined by Dr ___ based on outpatient count checks.\n\n# T1DM\nReasonably controlled at home on insulin. While on dex, sugars \nwere labile (both hypo and hyperglycemia) so ___ consulted \nand provided daily recommendations. On discharge, they \nrecommended return to home dosing with close outpatient followup \nwithin 1 week. ___ discharge team emailed to schedule apt, \nwho will call patient with details. \n\n# R. Heel Pressure Ulcer: \nContinued to appear uninfected during stay. Was discharged with \noutpatient ___ for continued wound care\n\n# Adrenal Insufficiency: \nHome prednisone was held during stay as he recieved \ndexamethasone. On discharge, prednisone resumed. \n\n# HTN:\nPatient's pressures remained stable off of medications. \n-Cont protonix\n\nTransitional Issues:\n1. Neulasta to be dosed ___. Will get count check and apt with \n___ same day\n2. Pt was discharged on daily levofloxacin prophylaxis in light \nof heel ulcer and recent neutropenic fever, with final duration \nto be determined by Dr ___ based on outpatient count \nchecks.\n3. Pt to continue prednisolone eye drops for 48 hrs post chemo.\n4. Pt would benefit from outpatient sleep study to assess \nwhether he has OSA and needs CPAP/BIPAP in addition to nasal \ncannula\n5. Pt needs close outpatient f/u regarding diabetes\n6. Pt needs to continue ongoing wound care of right heel via \n___.\n\nI personally spent 44 minutes coordinating care with outpatient \nproviders, educating patient, preparing discharge paperwork and \nanswering questions\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\n#Overnight Hypoxia\n#AML here for scheduled chemotherapy\n#T1DM complicated by hyper and hypoglycemia\n#R. Heel Pressure Ulcer: \n#Adrenal Insufficiency:",
